---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ContactInvitation from './ContactInvitation.astro';
import {getProjects,getCompanyFacts,getPageEditorial} from '../data/content';
import {companyReference} from '../data/company-reference';
import StructuredEditorial from './StructuredEditorial.astro';
import {glyphs} from '../data/brand';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import '../styles/editorial-detail.css';
import '../styles/editorial-expansion.css';
interface Props {draft?:boolean;}
const {draft=false}=Astro.props;
const projects=await getProjects(draft),facts=await getCompanyFacts(draft),editorial=await getPageEditorial('press',draft);
---
<Layout noindex={draft} title='Press & identity' description='NRTH Inc. company identity, the supplied NRTH wordmark and public resources for editorial use.'>
 {draft&&<aside class='preview-banner'><a href='/preview'>Editorial workspace</a><span data-preview-status>Draft preview</span></aside>}
 <section class='page-heading'><span class='section-label'>Press & identity</span><h1>The name is NRTH.<br/><em>The outlook is open.</em></h1><p>The company name, the supplied wordmark and a concise public reference. A consistent starting point for introducing NRTH and its venture directions.</p><a class='inline-link' href='#identity-resources'>Explore the identity resources</a></section>
 <section class='editorial-press-specimens' aria-label='The supplied NRTH wordmark in filled and outline forms'>
  <figure class='editorial-press-specimen'><svg viewBox='-6.5 -3 13 6' role='img' aria-label='The original four-letter NRTH wordmark'><g fill='currentColor'>{glyphs.map(d=><path d={d}/>)}</g></svg><figcaption>The wordmark. Four original letter shapes, held together.</figcaption></figure>
  <figure class='editorial-press-specimen'><svg viewBox='-6.5 -3 13 6' role='img' aria-label='The original NRTH wordmark shown as an outline'><g fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='.024' stroke-linejoin='round'>{glyphs.map(d=><path d={d}/>)}</g></svg><figcaption>The outline. The same contours, with a lighter presence.</figcaption></figure>
 </section>
 <section class='editorial-description-lengths' id='company-descriptions' aria-labelledby='description-title'><h2 id='description-title'>A sentence.<br/>An introduction.<br/>A fuller view.</h2><p>Public reference edition <time datetime={companyReference.edition}>October 12, 2026</time>. Choose the length that fits the context. These descriptions introduce the public identity and scope of the website.</p><div class='disclosure-list'>{companyReference.descriptions.map((description,i)=><details name='press-description-length' open={i===0}><summary>{description.length} description · {description.title}<Icon name='plus'/></summary><div>{description.paragraphs.map(paragraph=><p>{paragraph}</p>)}</div></details>)}</div><a class='inline-link' href='/resources/editorial-reference.txt' download>Download all three reference descriptions</a></section>
 <section class='editorial-reference-section' id='identity-resources'><div class='editorial-reference-heading'><h2>The essentials.<br/><em>Ready to reference.</em></h2><p>Use the scalable logo files for identity. The overview and text reference introduce the company and its public portfolio.</p></div><div class='editorial-resource-list'><a href='/resources/nrth-wordmark.svg' download><h3>The wordmark.</h3><p>The supplied NRTH letter shapes as a scalable vector. Use this file rather than recreating the name in a typeface.</p><span>Download SVG</span></a><a href='/resources/nrth-wordmark-outline.svg' download><h3>The outline.</h3><p>The same canonical contours as a vector outline, for layouts that call for a lighter treatment.</p><span>Download SVG</span></a><a href='/resources/nrth-company-overview.pdf' download><h3>The company view.</h3><p>A public introduction to NRTH Inc., the six fields and the nine venture identities in its portfolio.</p><span>Download PDF</span></a></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split section-dark'><div><span class='section-label'>Keep the identity clear</span><h2>A distinctive shape.<br/>A consistent name.</h2></div><div class='disclosure-list'><details open><summary>Preserve the original letter shapes.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>Use all four supplied glyphs: N, R, T and H. Keep their relative proportions, spacing and contours, including the open shape of the R. Scale the vector evenly rather than stretching or redrawing it.</p></details><details><summary>Give the wordmark room.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>Leave enough space around the mark to keep text, controls and imagery from competing with it. Choose a background with clear contrast and a size at which the letter shapes remain legible.</p></details><details><summary>Use the name precisely.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>NRTH Inc. is the company name. NRTH is the shorter brand name. nrth.group is the website domain. Venture identities use NRTH followed by the relevant venture name, such as NRTH Health or NRTH Systems.</p></details><details><summary>Describe the scope accurately.<Icon name='plus'/></summary><p>The public site introduces venture directions and illustrative contexts. Confirm product availability, commercial arrangements, milestones, technical integrations or other specific claims with NRTH before reporting them.</p></details></div></section>
 <section class='editorial-split'><div><span class='section-label'>Company reference</span><h2>NRTH Inc.</h2><p class='editorial-route-reference'>A short introduction that distinguishes the company from the website and individual venture identities.</p></div><div><div class='editorial-copy-reference'><p>NRTH Inc. brings nine venture directions together across mobility, health, systems, materials, events and research. NRTH is the shared company identity; nrth.group is its website. The portfolio considers the people, information, materials and coordination behind the work around us.</p></div><ul class='editorial-portfolio-reference'>{projects.map(project=><li><a href={'/projects/'+project.slug}>{project.name}</a></li>)}</ul><a class='inline-link' href='/resources/editorial-reference.txt' download>Download the company reference</a></div></section>
 <dl class='facts-list' aria-label='Company reference facts'>{facts.map(fact=><div><dt>{fact.label}</dt><dd>{fact.value}</dd></div>)}</dl>
 <section class='editorial-split section-dark'><div><span class='section-label'>Before publication</span><h2>Give the story<br/>its right context.</h2></div><div class='text-stack'><article><h3>Name the material.</h3><p>Identify whether you are covering a venture direction, an editorial perspective, a synthetic workflow or a visual design study. Include the relevant link and distinguish a public example from an actual product or completed engagement.</p></article><article><h3>Confirm the claim.</h3><p>For a development stage, availability, technical integration, partnership, company milestone or financial detail, request the current information and the person who can confirm its context. The public identity reference does not supply those separate facts.</p></article><article><h3>Make the inquiry specific.</h3><p>Share the subject, intended publication, information needed and deadline. A focused request makes it easier to identify the relevant venture and material.</p><a class='inline-link' href='/contact?topic=Press%20reference%20and%20claim%20confirmation'>Prepare an editorial inquiry</a></article></div></section>
 <StructuredEditorial editorial={editorial} id='press-detail' heading='More public reference materials.'/>
 <section class='resource-strip'><div><h3>A specific story needs a specific conversation.</h3><p>For interviews, venture details, identity questions or a company introduction, describe what you are covering and the context or deadline you are working with.</p></div><a class='inline-link' href='/contact?topic=Press%20%26%20identity'>Make a press inquiry</a></section>
 <ContactInvitation headline='Need a closer look?'/>
</Layout>
